# Privacy Policy

**Effective date: March 31, 2026**

The {SITE_NAME} Team ("we", "us", or "our") operates the {SITE_NAME} website (the "Service"). This page explains our practices regarding any information that may be involved when you use the Service.

We have designed {SITE_NAME} to be a privacy-respecting tool. **We do not require an account, we do not track you, and we do not store your content.**

---

## What Data We Collect

### Information you provide

{SITE_NAME} runs entirely in your browser. The username, comment text, and avatar you enter are used only to render a design mockup locally — this data is **never sent to our servers**.

### Technical & Anti-Abuse Data

Like most websites, our infrastructure logs standard HTTP request data. Additionally, to enforce daily free-tier limits and prevent automated abuse, we may generate a temporary, **non-identifiable device token** based on your IP address and browser metadata. This data is used strictly for rate limiting and security monitoring and is never sold or linked to any real-world identity.

---

## Cookies and Advertising

{SITE_NAME} uses minimal local storage for preferences. To support our free Service, we partner with Google AdSense and other third-party vendors. These vendors use cookies to serve ads based on your prior visits to our website or other websites on the internet.

Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to you based on your visit to our site. You may opt out of personalized advertising by visiting Google Ads Settings. You may also opt out of a third-party vendor's use of cookies for personalized advertising by visiting www.aboutads.info.

---

## How We Use Information

**Legal Basis for Processing:** We process your information based on our **legitimate interests** in securing our infrastructure, preventing service abuse, and fulfilling our commitment to provide a reliable service.

We use the minimal data described above only to:
- Deliver and maintain the Service (including enforcing daily export limits)
- Monitor for abuse, bot activity, or security incidents
- Diagnose and fix technical problems

We do **not** sell, rent, or share your data with third parties for marketing or advertising purposes.

California Privacy Rights (CCPA): We do not "sell" or "share" your personal information as defined by the CCPA. We do not use your sensitive personal information for any purposes other than to provide the Service.

International Data Transfers: Our Service is hosted globally. By using the Service, you acknowledge that your standard request data (like IP address) may be transferred to and processed in countries outside of your own, including the United States, where data protection laws may differ.

---

## Children's Privacy

{SITE_NAME} is not directed at children under the age of 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a child has submitted personal information through our Service, please contact us and we will promptly delete it.

---

## Payment Processing & Account Data

While the current version of the Service does not require account registration, future premium features may require you to provide an email address and payment information. In such cases, payment processing will be handled by secure third-party providers (e.g., Stripe), and we will not store your full credit card details.

When we transition to premium SaaS services, we will collect necessary account information (e.g., email address). We do not store your credit card information. All payments are processed by Stripe, who are independent Data Controllers. Their use of your personal information is governed by their respective Privacy Policies.
---

## Third-Party Services

The Service may link to or interact with the following third-party services:

| Service | Purpose | Their Privacy Policy |
|---|---|---|
| Cloudflare | Hosting and edge delivery | [cloudflare.com/privacypolicy](https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/) |
| Google AdSense | Advertising | [Google Adsense](https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads) |
| Stripe |	SaaS Subscriptions | [stripe](https://stripe.com/privacy) |

We are not responsible for the privacy practices of these third parties.

---

## Data Retention

Because we do not collect or store your comment content, usernames, or generated images, there is no user data for us to retain or delete.

---

## Your Rights

Depending on your jurisdiction, you may have rights regarding your personal data, including the right to access, correct, or delete it. Since we hold no personally identifiable information about you (beyond standard server logs), these rights are already effectively exercised by design.

To make a specific request, contact us via the channels below.

---

## Changes to This Policy

We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we do, we will revise the "Effective date" at the top of this page. We encourage you to review this page periodically.

---

